{"name":"Lemon Lime","hex":"#bffe28","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"lemon-lime","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["that contains a mixture of lemons and limes"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["a variety of citrus fruit","any lemon-lime drink"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lemon-lime"}],"entries":[{"title":"List of lemon-lime drink brands","blocks":[{"text":"A lemon-lime soft drink or lemon-lime soda is a carbonated soft drink with lemon and lime flavoring."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Cider_%28lemon-lime_drink%29.jpg/330px-Cider_%28lemon-lime_drink%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_lemon-lime_drink_brands","wikidata":"Q1130245"},{"title":"Lime (fruit)","blocks":[{"text":"A lime is the fruit of several species of citrus, most of which are hybrids within the genus Citrus. Limes are generally small, round to oval fruits with green flesh and skin and a distinctly sour taste due to their high citric acid content. They are widely cultivated in tropical and subtropical regions for culinary, medicinal, and ornamental purposes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/Lime_Blossom.jpg/330px-Lime_Blossom.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lime_(fruit)","wikidata":"Q13195"},{"title":"Lemon","blocks":[{"text":"The lemon is a species of small evergreen tree in the Citrus genus of the flowering plant family Rutaceae. A true lemon is a hybrid of the citron and the bitter orange. Its origins are uncertain, but some evidence suggests lemons originated during the 1st millennium BC in what is now northeastern India. Some other citrus fruits are called lemon."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/P1030323.JPG/330px-P1030323.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lemon","wikidata":"Q500"},{"title":"Lemon (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Lemon or lemon-color is a vivid yellow color characteristic of the lemon fruit. Shades of \"lemon\" may vary significantly from the fruit's actual color, including fluorescent tones and creamy hues reflective of lemon pies and confections."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Lemon_-_whole_and_split.jpg/330px-Lemon_-_whole_and_split.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lemon_(color)","wikidata":"Q2720565"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/e3/Sprite_%28drink%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/e3/Sprite_%28drink%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"Sprite","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASprite_(drink).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/7_Up_-_You_like_it%2C_it_likes_you%2C_1948.jpg/500px-7_Up_-_You_like_it%2C_it_likes_you%2C_1948.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/7_Up_-_You_like_it%2C_it_likes_you%2C_1948.jpg/1280px-7_Up_-_You_like_it%2C_it_likes_you%2C_1948.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/7_Up_-_You_like_it%2C_it_likes_you%2C_1948.jpg/500px-7_Up_-_You_like_it%2C_it_likes_you%2C_1948.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A 1948 7 Up magazine advertisement","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A7_Up_-_You_like_it%2C_it_likes_you%2C_1948.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/Limca_soft_dri